Dear APTITUDE partners,

On **28 October**, APTITUDE held its mid-term Periodic Review meeting in **Brussels**. The overall feedback was very positive. As we start Year 2, three priorities should guide our work: moving to implementation and piloting, working as one consortium, and making the value of APTITUDE tangible.

### 🔎 How the Review went

The Periodic Review gives the European Commission, HaDEA (European Health and Digital Executive Agency) and external experts an opportunity to assess the progress of the first reporting period and to discuss achievements, challenges and priorities directly with the consortium. For APTITUDE, it covered **October 2025 to September 2026**.

During the day, all Work Packages presented their progress, key achievements, deliverables and milestones, together with demonstrations and Member State perspectives. Discussions with the Commission and the external experts followed, and the day ended with a dedicated feedback session.

The work of our first year was recognised, with particular appreciation for the progress made across our use cases and for the quality of the work delivered. Thank you to the Work Package Leaders and to all partners who prepared the presentations and demonstrations.

### 🎯 Three priorities for Year 2

The Review also gave us a clear direction for the next phase: building on the work of Year 1 and turning it into a more integrated and user-oriented project.

- From preparation to implementation and piloting: in the coming months, we need to put our use cases into practice, test our solutions in real-world settings and learn from their implementation. The recent Board of Beneficiaries meeting had already identified piloting and deployment as central priorities for Year 2, and the Review confirmed them.
- Working as one consortium: APTITUDE's strength lies not only in the expertise and progress of each partner and Work Package, but in our ability to connect these contributions into a coherent whole. The Review highlighted the importance of stronger coordination and synergies across the project.
- Making the value of APTITUDE tangible: as pilots progress, we can show what the European Digital Identity (EUDI) Wallet concretely changes for citizens, businesses and public administrations, and turn technical achievements into solutions and benefits that people can understand and, ultimately, adopt. This focus on users and adoption is part of APTITUDE's overall objectives and should guide our work throughout Year 2.

Year 1 was about building the foundations. Year 2 is about putting them to work.

### 🤝 What this means for each partner

The Coordination Team will work with Work Package Leaders and partners to translate the Review feedback into concrete priorities and follow-up actions. But making Year 2 a success will be a collective effort, and every partner has a role to play. In practice, we count on each of you to:

- stay engaged in your Work Packages
- work with partners beyond your own area
- raise challenges early
- contribute actively to the pilots
- help capture and share results and lessons learned along the way

Let us now use what we have built together over the past year to make our pilots successful and show what APTITUDE can deliver. Thank you all for your continued commitment.

<br/>Best regards,
